      "content": "For the cooling stage of cooked poultry, you must cool it rapidly to below 41°F (5°C) within two hours. After that initial two hours, the temperature must continue to drop to 70°F (21°C) within an additional four hours. This two-stage cooling process is crucial to prevent the growth of pathogens like *Clostridium perfringens*. Remember, these time and temperature controls are vital for food safety.",
      "source": "target",
