      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's a common misconception, but these pathogens aren't just sitting there; they are actively *proliferating* like a swarm of tiny, hungry pests. Think of the Danger Zone as a feast where the bacteria are having a massive, unchecked party. *Clostridium perfringens*, for instance, thrives in conditions that are warm enough for it to be active but not so hot that it gets instantly killed. They are invisible, yes, but their activity is incredibly rapid when the temperature window is breached. Highlighting this active multiplication—not just passive presence—can help your staff grasp the urgency.",
